# Copy to .env.local (used by `npm run build` / `npm run preview`).
# Fill in the ApiEndpoint output from the backend stack.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-api-id.execute-api.ca-central-1.amazonaws.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# For `npm run dev`, ALSO create .env.development.local with the two lines below.
# Vite ranks .env.development.local above .env.local in dev mode, so these win there.
#
# Why: the deployed API allows exactly one CORS origin (the CloudFront domain), so calling it
# straight from http://localhost:5173 fails as "Failed to fetch". Pointing the app at a
# same-origin /api prefix lets vite.config.ts proxy the request in Node, where CORS doesn't
# apply -- without loosening the deployed API's allowlist. See docs/CONFIGURATION.md.
#
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
#   VITE_DEV_API_PROXY_TARGET=https://your-api-id.execute-api.ca-central-1.amazonaws.com
